{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## OPERATOR DECISION: restore real coverage on a representable field, and pin the refusal\n\nEscalated as NOT RESOLVABLE; operator ruled **option 1 + option 2**.\n\n**What this ticket now ships:**\n\n 1. **Rewrite the live cell to clear a NON-sub-task's parent** — a normal issue sitting under an\n    epic, whose parent is the \"Epic Link\" custom field. Jira permits nulling that field, so the cell\n    can actually reach rebar's clear path and prove it works against a real server. This is also the\n    closer analog to production, where most reconciled tickets are not sub-tasks.\n 2. **Keep a small assertion that DC still REFUSES the sub-task null** — so if a future Data Center\n    version starts allowing it, that check fails loudly and reopens the sub-task coverage question\n    instead of it being forgotten.\n\n**Rejected, with reasons recorded:** asserting the refusal ALONE (proves only that Jira still\nrefuses; gives no positive evidence our removal code works), and accepting unit-only coverage\n(rejected on this epic's own record — changes 1276 and 1288 both passed full unit suites and were\nstill wrong live, and 1288 destroyed 63 parent edges on its first production pass).\n\n**Dependency:** the rewrite uses the Epic Link clear path built by Gerrit **1311**, so it stacks on\nthat change rather than landing independently.\n\n**Two cheap falsifiers to fold into the same run**, since the NOT-RESOLVABLE verdict rests on\ndocumentation plus reported behaviour rather than a live experiment against this instance:\n * `GET /rest/api/2/issue/{subtask}/editmeta` — if `parent` exposes any operation beyond `set`, an\n   alternate clear exists and the verdict is wrong;\n * compare the `update`-verb form's error to the `fields` form's — a DIFFERENT error would mean the\n   verb form matters.\n\nIf either falsifier fires, the sub-task clear becomes representable after all and this ticket should\nbe reopened rather than closed on the rewrite alone."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785793600282467001,"uuid":"207db2d9-bb20-4262-a599-120bc1607d65"}